Pikachu is Pokémon's most iconic mascot and symbol. Among original 151 Pokémon, most popular include Charizard, Gengar, Bulbasaur, Eevee, Dragonite, Mew, Mewtwo, Arcanine, and Lapras. Other legendary fan-favorites: Greninja (Kalos), Mimikyu (Alola), Lucario (Sinnoh), and Umbreon (Johto). Popularity varies by region and generation. IGN ranked Bulbasaur #30, Metagross, and Arceus among their top 30. 2020 Pokémon of the Year poll (millions of global votes) showed Charizard, Greninja, Rayquaza, and Lucario as top favorites across regions. Design appeal, nostalgic factor (original generation), appearances in anime/merchandise, and competitive viability all influence popularity rankings.